  <section class="v58-dark v58-proof" id="proof">
    <div class="v58-wrap">
      <div class="v58-proof__head">
        <div><p class="v58-kicker"><span>\</span> How it works</p><h2>Move the bar. Watch the verdict move.</h2></div>
        <div class="v58-proof-intro">
          <p class="v58-lead">
            An anonymised AI-security candidate, scored on nine criteria. The interview evidence behind those scores
            never changes.
          </p>
          <p class="v58-lead v58-proof-intro__action">
            What changes is your brief. <span class="v58-proof-emphasis"
              >Set your priorities<svg viewBox="0 0 240 8" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"
                ><path d="M2 5 Q48 2 100 4 T181 3 Q219 2 238 4"></path></svg
              ></span
            > and the verdict follows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="v58-lab" data-v58-lab>
        <article class="v58-verdict">
          <div class="v58-verdict__who">
            <div><b>Bharat R.</b><span>AI Senior Security Engineer · 5 yrs · Bengaluru</span></div><em
              data-band
              data-band-state="select">SELECT</em
            >
          </div>
          <div class="v58-verdict__score"><b data-verdict-score>39.00</b><span>/ 50</span></div>
          <div class="v58-verdict__track"><i></i><i></i><i></i><b data-pin></b></div><p class="v58-verdict__axis">
            <span>0</span><span>Reject · 26 · Grey · 34 · Select</span><span>50</span>
          </p>
          <p class="v58-side-label">Individual scores · <strong>out of 5</strong></p>
          <div class="v58-score-tiles">
            {
              rubricDimensions.map(([, label, short, score]) => (
                <span
                  tabindex="0"
                  role="group"
                  aria-label={`${label}: evidence score ${score} out of 5`}
                  title={`${label}: ${score} out of 5`}
                  class:list={{ low: score === 2 }}
                >
                  <>
                    <i>{short}</i>
                    <b>{score}</b>
                  </>
                </span>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <p class="v58-verdict__note" data-note>
            As briefed: building production detection systems carries the weight. AI security controls are the evidence
            to probe further.
          </p>
        </article>
        <div class="v58-controls">
          <div class="v58-mobile-verdict" aria-label="Current verdict">
            <span>Current verdict</span><strong data-mobile-score>39.00 <small>/ 50</small></strong><em
              data-mobile-band
              data-band-state="select">SELECT</em
            >
          </div><p class="v58-sr-status" role="status" aria-atomic="true" data-verdict-status></p><p
            class="v58-side-label"
          >
            Choose a brief
          </p><div class="v58-presets" role="group" aria-label="Weighting presets">
            <button type="button" class="is-active" data-preset="brief" aria-pressed="true">As briefed</button><button
              type="button"
              data-preset="detection"
              aria-pressed="false">Detection first</button
            ><button type="button" data-preset="llm" aria-pressed="false">LLM security</button><button
              type="button"
              data-preset="ownership"
              aria-pressed="false">Ownership</button
            >
          </div><div class="v58-weights-panel">
            <p class="v58-weight-instruction" id="weight-instruction">
              Adjust the sliders to set what matters most.
            </p><div class="v58-priorities-heading">
              <h3 class="v58-priorities-title">Your priorities</h3><span>Importance</span>
            </div><div class="v58-priority-rows">
              {
                rubricDimensions.map(([code, label, , score, weight]) => (
                  <label data-row>
                    <>
                      <i>{code}</i>
                      <span>{label}</span>
                      <input
                        type="range"
                        min="0"
                        max="12"
                        step="0.25"
                        value={weight}
                        data-default={weight}
                        data-score={score}
                        aria-label={`Importance of ${label}`}
                        aria-describedby="weight-instruction"
                      />
                      <b data-share>{(Number(weight) * 2).toFixed(1)}%</b>
                    </>
                  </label>
                ))
              }
            </div><p class="v58-share-status" data-share-status hidden>
              Move a slider above zero to set your priorities.
            </p><details class="v58-calculation">
              <summary>How the score is calculated</summary><p>
                Each skill contributes its share of importance multiplied by the candidate's evidence score out of 5.
                The result is expressed out of 50.
              </p><p>
                Displayed shares are rounded to total 100% when priorities are set. Scoring uses exact shares.
              </p><table>
                <thead
                  ><tr><th scope="col">Skill</th><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">Points / 50</th></tr
                  ></thead
                ><tbody
                  >{
                    rubricDimensions.map(([, label, , score, weight]) => (
                      <tr>
                        <>
                          <th scope="row">{label}</th>
                          <td>{score}/5</td>
                          <td data-calculated-points>{((Number(weight) * score) / 5).toFixed(2)}</td>
                        </>
                      </tr>
                    ))
                  }</tbody
                >
              </table>
            </details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="v58-proof__closure">
        <p class="v58-lab-foot">Tell us what matters most. <em>This is what we recalibrate.</em></p><div
          class="v58-proof-checks"
        >
          <div><h3>Every score points to the exact line behind it.</h3><p>Evidence you can review.</p></div><div>
            <h3>We name what we didn't test.</h3><p>So your own round knows exactly where to look.</p>
          </div><div>
            <h3>Resume claims checked against the evidence.</h3><p>
              Experience, skills and the work behind each claim.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

